[SO-16197226] Q: How to enable Code First Migrations in ASP MVC app?
A: <p>In the Package Manager Console, if you run <code>Get-Help Enable-Migrations</code>, it will show you all of the advanced options.  Included in those are:</p>

<ul>
<li>-ProjectName (the project to run this command against, i.e. to look for the context type)</li>
<li>-StartupProjectName (the project which has the app.config/web.config where the context runs, i.e. where your connection string lives).  <strong>This one is important unless your Model project has the correct connection string in its own .config file.</strong></li>
<li>-ConnectionString (the connection string to use while scaffolding the migration if you want to override the value)</li>
</ul>

<p>When you're using <code>Add-Migration</code> it should support the same options.</p>

<p>You can also change the Package Manager Console's Default Project dropdown to run against your model project by default.</p>


