<p>Your cPanel username and password can be used to connect to your databases (as well as your cPanel). If you're connecting to your database using your cPanel username and password, you can reset your cPanel password to ensure you are using the correct username and password.</p>
<p>If you setup a MySQL username and password specifically for accessing a database, you'll want to ensure you are using the correct username in your php scripts. For example, MySQL usernames are always in this format:</p>
<p>cpanel-username_mysql-username</p>
<p>If your cPanel username is userna5 and you created a database username of dbuser1, then the actual database username would be:</p>
<p>userna5_dbuser1</p>
